# provenance: PV-0124
# kind: support-bits
# description: A SUPPORTDATA mask one byte short of the required 32 bytes.
# derivation: The mask is exactly 32 bytes (PV-0124); the input stops after 31 bytes, one byte short of the mask, so the decode is truncated. The set bits are otherwise valid, so the length is the only fault.
# expect.error: truncated
hex:
81                     # byte 0
00 00 00 00 00 00 00   # bytes 1-7
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 # bytes 8-15
80 20 00 00 00 00 20   # bytes 16-22
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 # bytes 23-30 (only 8 -> total 31 bytes)
